{"name":"Badlands Orange","hex":"#ff6316","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"badlands","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An arid terrain characterized by severe erosion of sedimentary rocks.","An arid region of Western Canada characterized by significant erosion and odd land formations containing dinosaur and other fossils."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/badlands"},{"term":"orange","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree of the genus Citrus such as Citrus sinensis which yields oranges (the fruit).","Any round citrus fruit with a yellow-red colour when ripe and a sour-sweet taste; the fruit of the orange tree.\n Specifically, a sweet orange or Citrus sinensis."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of the fruit of an orange tree; yellowred; reddish-yellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange"}],"entries":[{"title":"Badlands","blocks":[{"text":"Badlands are a type of dry terrain where softer sedimentary rocks and clay-rich soils have been extensively eroded. They are characterized by steep slopes, minimal vegetation, lack of a substantial regolith, and high drainage density. Ravines, gullies, buttes, hoodoos and other such geologic forms are common in badlands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Chinle_Badlands.jpg/330px-Chinle_Badlands.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Badlands","wikidata":"Q272921"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(colour)","wikidata":"Q39338"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/A030%2C_Theodore_Roosevelt_National_Park%2C_North_Dakota%2C_USA%2C_2001.jpg/330px-A030%2C_Theodore_Roosevelt_National_Park%2C_North_Dakota%2C_USA%2C_2001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/A030%2C_Theodore_Roosevelt_National_Park%2C_North_Dakota%2C_USA%2C_2001.jpg/330px-A030%2C_Theodore_Roosevelt_National_Park%2C_North_Dakota%2C_USA%2C_2001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Caprock atop hoodoos in Theodore Roosevelt National Park, North Dakota, U.S.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA030%2C_Theodore_Roosevelt_National_Park%2C_North_Dakota%2C_USA%2C_2001.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Cheltenham_Badlands_panorama1.jpg/500px-Cheltenham_Badlands_panorama1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Cheltenham_Badlands_panorama1.jpg/1280px-Cheltenham_Badlands_panorama1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Cheltenham_Badlands_panorama1.jpg/500px-Cheltenham_Badlands_panorama1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cheltenham Badlands, Caledon, Canada","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACheltenham_Badlands_panorama1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Linze%2C_Zhangye%2C_Gansu%2C_China_-_panoramio_%284%29.jpg/500px-Linze%2C_Zhangye%2C_Gansu%2C_China_-_panoramio_%284%29